# Milestone: M3
# Covers: row 11 §3.2 — the unwind_value carried by UEXEC_TAG_STOP is opaque
#         to urbiscript; no surface exists to read the in-flight value from
#         inside an onleave handler or a finally block.
#
# defer-to: M5
#
# Reason: requires onleave clause parse/emit (M5 reactive runtime) and
# tag.stop(value) surface syntax (M4 object model).  At M3, the unwind_value
# field exists in UStrand but there is no urbiscript expression that can
# read it.  This is a language-semantics assertion (the value is intentionally
# hidden from user code) and can only be tested once onleave clauses exist.
#
# When M5 lands, implement this fixture by uncommenting the source below.
# Expected behaviour: onleave body cannot read the stop value; trying to
# reference it results in nil / no-binding, not the actual passed value.
#
# Urbiscript source (activate at M5):
#   var t = Tag.new;
#   var seen = nil;
#   t: { 1 } onleave { seen = stopValue };
#   t.stop("secret");
#   seen
#   --- expected output (value is opaque, stopValue is unbound → nil) ---
#   [00000001] nil
